  "id": "Compound::DB00306 - Gene::2554",
  "verbalization": "Talbutal is likely to interact with Gabra1 through a shared mechanism involving Gaba-a receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Talbutal binds to Gabre or Gabrq, which in turn participate in Gaba-a receptor activity, ultimately leading to Gabra1 being involved in this process. The varying target proteins (Gabra1, Gabrb1, and Gabrq) indicate that Talbutal may engage with different subunits of the Gaba-a receptor, potentially modulating its function. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the specific molecular interaction may differ based on the target subunit. The integration of these pathways highlights a role for Talbutal in influencing Gaba-a receptor activity, which could have implications for its pharmacological effects and therapeutic applications.",
